          "rationale": "For the original transformation, solving T(x,y,z)=0 gives equations 2x-4y+2z=0, x-3y+z=0, and 4x-4y+z=0. Subtracting twice the second equation from the first gives 2y=0. Subtracting four times the second equation from the third gives 8y-3z=0, hence z=0 and then x=0. Therefore Ker(T)={(0,0,0)}, original option b (index 1). This derived judgment agrees with the authentic worked solution and saved Correct grading. The stored bmatrix and captured bracketed aligned vector preserve the same singleton set and ordered entries."
