    {
      "question": "e-5440",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "495367894a4185a7495501320ca727276508445c535bf7ffa028b35d1d56f548",
      "new_sha256": "0d57d7974a834af0f450e00853a68f308163683d7b61d8152a60c350b5a4fef3",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-5440",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "First, we write down the standard matrix of $\\mathbf{T}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071281/assets/f27d3195556ff8786f9416cddbe4ad52cf1838f2b0ce37b4da11746fee59fb9c.png)\n\nRecall that $\\textrm{nullity}(\\mathbf{T}) = \\textrm{nullity}(T) = \\textrm{dim}(\\textrm{Null}(T)).$\n\nIn order to find $\\textrm{dim}(\\textrm{Null}(T)),$ we reduce $T$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 10 & -1 \\\\ -6 & -12 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -6 & -12 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has no non-pivot columns. Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\textrm{nullity}(\\mathbf{T})=\\textrm{dim}(\\textrm{Null}(T))=0.\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071281/example-5440.json",
